From: Diogo Trindade <diogotr7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd939x-sdw: ignore RX device interrupts

Only the TX device has a regmap and the interrupt domain, so an alert from
the RX device dereferences a NULL regmap and kills the bus IRQ thread.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c
@@ -196,6 +196,9 @@ static int wcd9390_interrupt_callback(struct sdw_slave *slave,
 {
 	struct wcd939x_sdw_priv *wcd = dev_get_drvdata(&slave->dev);
 
+	if (!wcd->is_tx)
+		return 0;
+
 	return wcd_interrupt_callback(slave, wcd->slave_irq, WCD939X_DIGITAL_INTR_STATUS_0,
 			WCD939X_DIGITAL_INTR_STATUS_1, WCD939X_DIGITAL_INTR_STATUS_2);
 }
